  "findings": "Compared the wild-form photograph by David J. Stang, then all three refined sizes and the current 36-sheet. Broad basal rosettes and individual flower stalks remain legible across compact, spreading and leaning clumps. Purple double-flower cultivars were excluded from species/color judgment. Coarse opaque 25 mm petals and the existing stronger yellow palette are recorded stylization limits; leaf wrinkling and pale cream species coloring await the separate appearance pass.",
